{
  "analysis": "I'm starting fresh in the /workspace directory. I can see there's a gen_inputs.py, setup.sh, an inputs directory, and a skill_context directory. I need to explore these to understand the task requirements and available inputs before generating the sprint planning package.",
  "plan": "First, I'll explore the workspace structure to understand what's available. I'll check the skill_context directory for documentation, look at the inputs folder, and see if there's a synthesize_task.py script or if I need to generate inputs first.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la inputs/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/skill.md 2>/dev/null || cat skill_context/*.md 2>/dev/null\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "I can see the workspace structure. There's a skill_context/SKILL.md file with agile product owner guidance, and an inputs folder with backlog_seed.json, product_brief.json, and marker_note.txt. The skill.md content was truncated. I need to read the full documentation and input files.",
  "plan": "Read the full SKILL.md documentation, then examine all input files to understand the backlog items, product brief, and marker notes that need to be preserved.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "The SKILL.md is truncated in output. I need to read the input files to understand the backlog items and product brief. Let me examine the inputs folder content.",
  "plan": "Read all input files (backlog_seed.json, product_brief.json, marker_note.txt) to understand the data I need to work with, then read more of the SKILL.md documentation.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat inputs/backlog_seed.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat inputs/product_brief.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat inputs/marker_note.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -200 skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "I now have the key input data:\n- 5 backlog items (ONB-101 to ONB-105) with personas, needs, benefits, and complexity hints\n- Product brief with epic name, business goal, team velocity (29), availability factor (0.9), sprint days (10)\n- Constraints: max 85% capacity, testable acceptance criteria, no story >8 points, 10% buffer\n- Marker: PO-MARKER-7F3A\n\nI need to read more of the SKILL.md to understand INVEST criteria and acceptance criteria patterns.",
  "plan": "Read more of the SKILL.md documentation to understand INVEST criteria, acceptance criteria patterns (Given-When-Then), and story point estimation guidelines.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "tail -n +200 skill_context/SKILL.md | head -200\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -A 30 'INVEST' skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -A 20 'Given-When-Then' skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "I'm getting more useful information. I see sprint planning templates with capacity calculations and priority levels. I need to see the full INVEST criteria table and acceptance criteria patterns.",
  "plan": "Continue reading SKILL.md to get the complete INVEST criteria and acceptance criteria patterns, then check the references folder for additional guidance.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -A 50 'INVEST Criteria Validation' skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -A 30 'Acceptance Criteria' skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/references/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/references/*.md 2>/dev/null | head -100\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}
